"Using the Yoto App on iOS and Android (https://support.yotoplay.com/en_gb/using-the-yoto-app-on-ios-and-android-ryJtFi7Me)\nciteturn816search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3 months ago; Crawled: last week; Right Button Shortcuts - By default, your player will play Yoto Daily and Yoto Radio on first and second press during the day; and Yoto Sleep Radio on first press during the night.\n\nFrom the Maxi Player, you can also: \n\n  * Set a sleep timer by tapping on the moon and stars icon in the right-hand corner.\n  * Choose the playback speed, rewind/ forward within the chapter by 15 seconds or by using the slider at the top.\n  * See the chapters of a card by pressing on the burger menu..\n\nDiscover tab\n\nImage: Yoto App - Discover tab\n\nThis is where you'll find and discover all of our free content covering radio, podcasts, sleep and stories. You can play all content from here and if you like it, you can add it to your own library for fast access. Just tap on the content to see the content details and tap 'Add to library'.\n\nSettings tab\n\nImage: Yoto App - Settings tabThis is where you can see details of who is in your Family Account and all of your players.\n\nYour registered details are at the top of the screen (this is the email address you used to sign in to the app). You will also be able to see details of all users (including you) in your Family Account who are paired with your players.\n\nUnder the list of users, you will also see all the players linked to your Family Account. \n\nEach listed player has a chevron icon. Tap this icon to manage settings for that player. \n\nSTATUS\n\nPlayer name - Personalize your player by giving it a name\n\nBattery level - view battery level of your player\n\nManage Wi-Fi - disconnect your player from the Wi-Fi or add a new network\n\nAudio Download Status - This shows you if all your cards have been downloaded to your player, or if some content still needs to download. If content is not downloaded fully, it will need to stream, which may cause playback issues if you have poor Wi-Fi in the location of your player\n\nALARMS\n\nSet-up up to 10 alarms. \n\nDAY AND NIGHT MODE\n\nMorning - Set a start time for day mode (the clock will change from moon to sun)\n\nBedtime - Set a start time for night mode (your clock will change from sun to moon)\n\nMorning Light / Nightlight Color (V2/V3 only) - Choose the color of the light on the rear of the Player. You can set different colors for night and day, so your child knows when it’s time to get up, even if the player is on its front. Only for Yoto Player: the Yoto Mini does not have a night light.\n\nAuto Display Brightness (V3 only) - Enable the Display Brightness to be auto-adjusted based on ambient light.\n\nDisplay Brightness - Set the default screen brightness during day/night modes when Auto Display Brightness is disabled/unavailable.\n\nVolume Limit - Set a limit for how loud your player will go for the day/night modes.\n\nNote: this volume limit applies to the Speaker and Wired Headphone outputs. The Yoto Wireless Headphones feature their own kid-safe volume limiting.\n\nRight Button Shortcuts - By default, your player will play Yoto Daily and Yoto Radio on first and second press during the day; and Yoto Sleep Radio on first press during the night. These can be edited to include French Language items and Timers. \n\nADVANCED\n\nBattery saver - Set how quickly the player display dims when no buttons or cards are touched, and when not on the dock. \n\nAuto Power-Off - Set how quickly the player switched off when no buttons or cards are touched while off charge. \n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHow to control your Yoto player (https://support.yotoplay.com/en_gb/how-to-control-your-yoto-player-SyGKKj7zg)\nciteturn816search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: last month; Crawled: last week; ### Power button – bottom-right corner on Yoto Player (4th Generation); top-right corner on Yoto Mini (4th Generation) ... Pro tip: you can customise what the right-hand dial does in day and night mode from the Yoto App - head to your player’s settings tab.\n\n## How to control your Yoto player\n\nSeptember 10 2026 12:19pm • Est. Read Time: 2 MIN\n\nWhen nothing is playing and the clock is showing, press the Green Button to play the first item on the Green Button menu (default set to Yoto Daily). \n\n### Every player keeps it simple: turn, press, or hold. Find your model below for exactly what each button does.\n\n## 4th Generation controls\n\n### Left orange button\n\n  * Turn to adjust the volume.\n\n  * Short press to skip to the previous track.\n\n  * Press and hold to rewind.\n\n  * When the clock is showing, press and hold to pair Bluetooth headphones.\n\n### Right orange button\n\n  * Turn to navigate through tracks, then press to select one.\n\n  * Short press to skip to the next track.\n\n  * Press and hold to fast-forward.\n\n### The Green Button\n\n  * Twist to browse your child’s favourites - the artwork appears on the display - then press to play.\n\n  * When nothing is playing and the clock is showing, press the Green Button to play the first item on the Green Button menu (default set to Yoto Daily). \n\n  * Note: A grown-up chooses what’s on the Green Button first, in the Yoto App. See: Using the Green Button. \n\n### Power button – bottom-right corner on Yoto Player (4th Generation); top-right corner on Yoto Mini (4th Generation)\n\n  * Long press to turn your player on or off.\n\n  * Short press to check the battery level.\n\n## Earlier players controls\n\n### Left orange dial (Yoto Player and Yoto Mini)\n\n  * Turn clockwise or anti-clockwise to adjust the volume.\n\n  * Press to skip to the previous track or chapter (with a card in).\n\n  * Press and hold (longer than 1 second) while something’s playing to rewind.\n\n  * Press and hold for about 3 seconds with the clock showing to open the Bluetooth menu - then turn the right-hand dial to choose and press to confirm. [LINK PLACEHOLDER - Using headphones with your Yoto]\n\n### Right orange dial (Yoto Player and Yoto Mini)\n\nWith a card in:\n\n  * Press to skip to the next track or chapter.\n\n  * Turn to navigate forwards or backwards through tracks and chapters.\n\n  * Press and hold (longer than 1 second) while something’s playing to fast-forward.\n\nWith no card in:\n\n  * Press once to play Yoto Daily (when you’re online).\n\n  * Press again for Yoto Radio - and once more to return to the clock.\n\nYoto Player only - nightlight mode (player face down):\n\n  * Turn clockwise to brighten the nightlight (or turn it back on from zero), anti-clockwise to dim it down to zero.\n\nPro tip: you can customise what the right-hand dial does in day and night mode from the Yoto App - head to your player’s settings tab.\n\n### Power button\n\nYou’ll find it on the right side of Yoto Player (3rd Generation) and Yoto Mini, and in the bottom right-hand corner of Yoto Player (2nd Generation).\n\nPress…  | What happens\nShort press  | Pauses or resumes the audio - including audio playing from the app\nLong press  | Stops the audio\nHold for about 3 seconds  | Turns the player on or off. On Yoto Player: the nightlight flashes twice as it turns on, and a white Yoto face appears as it turns off\nHold for 10 seconds  | Hard reset - restarts a frozen or misbehaving player. Your Wi-Fi details and audio are safe\n\n## How fast-forward and rewind speed up\n\nThe longer you hold either dial, the faster you move through the audio - the chevrons (>) on the display tell you how fast:\n\nHold for…  | You’ll see  | Speed\nLonger than 1 second  | >>  | 20 seconds of audio per second\nAfter 4 seconds  | >>>  | 50 seconds per second\nAfter 7 seconds  | >>>>  | 120 seconds per second\n\n## If a button isn’t responding\n\nContact our Customer Happiness team, we’d love to help.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n4th Generation Yoto player FAQs (https://support.yotoplay.com/en_gb/4th-generation-yoto-player-faqs-Byw2rlFzx)\nciteturn816search2 [wordlim: 200] Published: last month; Crawled: today; It shares many of the same great Yoto features as Player, including the new Green Button, giving kids quick access to personal playlists of up to 20 titles for day and night, even when their Yoto Cards aren't to hand. ... By default, that’s Yoto Daily during the day and Yoto Sleep Radio at night. ... On previous generations of Yoto Player, a single press of the right-hand button provides this quick-access function.\nIt shares many of the same great Yoto features as Player, including the new Green Button, giving kids quick access to personal playlists of up to 20 titles for day and night, even when their Yoto Cards aren't to hand. Instead of the Yoto Player's full-panel night light, Mini prioritises portability and durability, with an IP67 water and dust-resistant design that's ready for the rough and tumble of childhood.\n\n## How does the Green Button work?\n\nThe Green Button gives kids quick access to their favourite audio, no Yoto Card needed. Just twist to browse and press to play.\n\nThere are two playlists: one for daytime and one for night time, each holding up to 20 titles. Yoto Daily and Yoto Radio are included in the daytime playlist by default, with Yoto Sleep Radio ready for night time.\n\nGrown-ups can customise both playlists in the Yoto App, adding audio from their library including stories, music, podcasts, radio stations, soundscapes, timers, sleep sounds and even your own recordings.\n\nOnce added, compatible audio downloads to the player, so kids can browse and listen even when they’re offline or on the move. Some audio, including radio stations and podcasts, requires an internet connection to stream.\n\nUsing the Green Button is simple:\n\n  * Twist to browse through titles and see their artwork on the display.\n\n  * Press to play the title you’ve chosen.\n\n  * Press again to pause.\n\n  * Press and hold to eject the audio and return to the clock.\n\n  * Press when no audio is playing to instantly play the first title in the current day or night playlist. By default, that’s Yoto Daily during the day and Yoto Sleep Radio at night.\n\nGrown-ups can change which title appears first in either playlist at any time in the Yoto App.\n\nOn previous generations of Yoto Player, a single press of the right-hand button provides this quick-access function.\n\n## What is the difference between the old and new Yoto players?\n\nYoto Player and Yoto Mini 4th Gen offer kids more choice, are more personal and are better equipped for family life.\n\n  * More choice for kids: The new Green Button and Day & Night Modes give kids even more independence over their listening, letting them twist straight to their favourites – handy when their favourite Yoto Card “must be here somewhere”.\n\n  * Made for family routines: Day & Night Modes make it easy to have different favourites ready for different parts of the day – from Yoto Daily over breakfast to sleep sounds at bedtime. There are handy features like toothbrush timers too, while Yoto Player's new full-panel night light gives families even more ways to set the mood for bedtime, wake-up and everything in between. And Yoto Mini is ready to come along for it all, with IP67 water and dust resistance for the rough and tumble of childhood.\n\n  * A big upgrade on the inside, too: We've overhauled the technology inside both players, informed by feedback from our community of Yoto families. Audio downloads to the player faster, interactions feel more responsive, and improved Wi-Fi and Bluetooth connectivity make connecting to the Yoto App and Bluetooth headphones smoother and more reliable.\n\nAnd there's more to come. The new technology inside 4th Gen gives us greater scope to develop the Yoto experience over time, bringing new features and enhancements to Yoto Player and Yoto Mini.\n\n## What is the display for?\n\nThe display brings a visual dimension to Yoto's audio-first experience. Title artwork helps kids browse and choose what they want to listen to using the Green Button - much like picking a Yoto Card from their card case - while pixel icons help them navigate chapters and tracks as they listen.\n\nWhen audio isn't playing, the display also works as a clock, with customisable day and night settings that can help with family routines - including acting as an okay-to-wake cue.\n\n## What else do I get when I buy a Yoto player?\n\nThere's plenty to get you started! Every Yoto Player and Yoto Mini comes with a USB-C charging cable and a Welcome Card, which doubles as your first Make Your Own Card. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nUsing your Yoto as a nightlight (https://support.yotoplay.com/en_gb/using-your-yoto-as-a-nightlight-r1BYtjXfg)\nciteturn816search3 [wordlim: 200] Published: last month; Crawled: today; You can set a different colour for Day and Night mode - a lovely okay-to-wake cue for little ones who can’t read the clock yet: one colour means it’s still sleep time, another means it’s fine to get up. ... Please also note that selecting content on the Green Button is disabled when the nightlight is on. ...   * Yoto Mini does not have a nightlight, but it does have a Day and Night mode!\n\n## Using your Yoto as a nightlight\n\n### Turn your Yoto Player onto its front, and the nightlight comes on. Stand it upright, and it’s off. But there’s a little more to it… \n\nOne quick tip: flip it on a hard, flat surface like a bedside table. Avoid carpeted floors or beds.\n\n### Adjusting the brightness\n\nWhile the player is face down, twist the right-hand orange dial - left to dim (all the way down to off), right to brighten.\n\nYoto Player (4th Generation) adjusts itself: its auto-brightness dims the nightlight to match the light in the room. Twisting the dial overrides it for the night - stand the player upright and pop it back down, and auto-brightness takes over again.\n\n### Changing the colour\n\nPick your nightlight colour in the Yoto App: go to the Settings tab and tap the arrow icon next to your player.\n\nYou can set a different colour for Day and Night mode - a lovely okay-to-wake cue for little ones who can’t read the clock yet: one colour means it’s still sleep time, another means it’s fine to get up. \n\nWhile the nightlight is on - Yoto Player (4th Generation)\n\nThe display switches off so it doesn’t light up the room. Your child can still:\n\n  * Play and pause audio\n\n  * Change the volume\n\n  * Skip through tracks\n\nPlease also note that selecting content on the Green Button is disabled when the nightlight is on.\n\n### Good to know\n\n  * Yoto Player (3rd Generation): the room-temperature sensor takes a break while the player is in nightlight mode.\n\n  * Yoto Mini does not have a nightlight, but it does have a Day and Night mode! --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHow to remove a user from your Family Account (https://support.yotoplay.com/en_gb/how-to-remove-a-user-from-your-family-account-H162uFjmfl)\nciteturn816search4 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3 months ago; Crawled: 3 weeks ago;   * Open the Yoto App\n\n## How to remove a user from your Family Account\n\nJuly 20 2026 9:14am\n\nEach member of a Family Account can either remove themselves or remove other users.\nTo remove a user from a Family Account:\n\n  * Open the Yoto App\n  * Go to the Settings tab\n  * Tap the three dots menu next to a user\n  * This will show the menu with the remove options\n  * Select either Remove from Family Account or Leave this Family Account--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nComment utiliser l’Appli Yoto (https://support.yotoplay.com/fr/comment-utiliser-l%27appli-yoto-ryJtFi7Me)\nciteturn816search5 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3 months ago; Crawled: last week; Visitez la boutique Yoto où vous pourrez découvrir un florilège de cartes audio.\n\n#### ALARMES\n\nConfigurez jusqu’à 10 alarmes. Pour en savoir plus, cliquez ici.\n\n#### \n\n#### MODE JOUR ET NUIT\n\nHeure du matin : définissez une heure pour indiquer le mode jour (l’horloge passera de la lune au soleil)\n\nHeure du coucher : définissez une heure pour indiquer le mode nuit (l’horloge passera du soleil à la lune)\n\nVeilleuse : choisissez la couleur de la veilleuse. Vous pouvez choisir des couleurs différentes pour le mode jour et le mode nuit, afin que votre enfant sache quand il est l’heure de se lever (même si le lecteur est sur sa face avant et qu’ils ne peuvent pas voir l’horloge). Uniquement pour les utilisateurs du Yoto Player.\n\nLuminosité et affichage : vous pouvez ajuster la luminosité de votre lecteur automatiquement ou manuellement.\n\nLimite du Volume maximum : définissez une limite pour le volume sonore de votre lecteur en mode jour et en mode nuit.\n\nRaccourcis bouton droit : par défaut, votre lecteur jouera Mini Journal et Radio Yoto au premier et au deuxième clic en mode jour ; et Radio Douce Nuit au premier clic en mode nuit. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nYoto player software (OS) updates (https://support.yotoplay.com/en_gb/yoto-player-software-%28os%29-updates-ByglYKimze)\nciteturn816search6 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 days ago;   * Fixed Right Hand Button content ejecting when a player moves between Day/Night mode ...   * Fixed deep sleep issue when Yoto Mini is at lowest battery ...   * Any button press can be used to cancel a sounding alarm\n\n## Yoto player software (OS) updates\n\n#### What's new in the latest Yoto OS release!\n\nTip: you can check which Yoto OS version your player is running in the Yoto app by going to Account and tapping the Settings icon next to your player \n\n#### Latest releases\n\nYoto OS v2.23.3 (10th December 2025)\n\n  * Improvements to power consumption when a device is in deep sleep mode\n  * Note: This OS version is currently available only on the latest production batch of players, where the underlying issue has been fixed. There are no changes for earlier devices which are running v2.23.2.\n\nYoto OS v2.23.2 (29th September 2025)\n\n  * Improved setup when connecting to new Wi-Fi network\n  * Battery saver display will no longer dim during FF/RW\n  * Improved Right Hand Button behaviour when pausing and when player is offline\n  * Fixed issue for players reporting incorrect charge status with underpowered chargers\n  * Nightlight brightness amount is saved & recalled correctly (Yoto Player 3rd Generation only)\n\nYoto OS v2.22.6 (21st July 2025)\n\n  * Supported lowering brightness when idle and disconnected from Wi-Fi\n  * Fixed a memory management issue which was causing NFC failures\n\nYoto OS v2.22.5 (23rd June 2025)\n\n  * Added support for dynamic icons in the Weather App\n  * Support for the Yoto Developer Program - to find out more visit https://yoto.dev/\n  * Fix for Animated Icons\n\nYoto OS v2.22.4 (4th June 2025)\n\n  * Implemented Fast Forward/Rewind - simply hold down the left or right buttons while playing audio to start scrubbing forwards or backwards!\n  * Fixed issue with out-of-date Yoto Daily episodes\n  * Fixed playback issues with Yoto Radio\n  * Fixed issue where Yoto BT headphone - and + buttons do not skip track/chapters\n  * Improved internal tools to support customers\n  * Fixed Right Hand Button content ejecting when a player moves between Day/Night mode\n  * Improved card deletion to free space\n  * Fixed nightlight brightness not adjusting while audio is playing\n\nYoto OS v2.21.9 (7th April 2025)\n\n  * Fixed an issue where Yoto Daily wouldn't show today's date\n  * Improvements for Right Hand Button behaviour\n  * Improvements to collecting Player crashes and performance\n  * Fixed issue playing non downloaded gif content\n  * Fixed Headphone port failure/crash\n  * Fixed issue where plays from the app initially trigger the last-played track\n  * Fixed issue where first card insert is not registered and idle screen locks up\n  * Other minor bugfixes and improvements\n\nYoto OS v2.21.4 (19th February 2025)\n\n  * Improvements for Bluetooth Headphones\n    * Volume limit now applies when changing volume from headphones\n    * Fixed Pre/Next buttons from Bluetooth Headphones\n  * Improvements to audio playback\n    * Improved playback reporting to the app\n    * Support for Opus audio codec\n  * Improved retry logic for failed downloads\n  * Various fixes for bugs and crashes\n\nYoto OS V.2.11.1 (18th January 2023)\n\n  * Prevent screen turning from off during pairing process\n  * Improvements to testing framework\n  * Fixed issue with wired headphones playing over volume limit when Bluetooth headphones are also connected\n  * aw881xx watchdog timeout workaround for Mini player\n  * UX improvements for the Bluetooth menu\n  * Bluetooth: fix enabling Bluetooth for the first time\n\nYoto OS v2.10.7 (21st November 2022)\n\n  * Optimize Wi-Fi power consumption when disconnected\n  * Optimize NFC power consumption when auto power-off is enabled\n  * Fix audio synchronization of startup jingle sound and animation\n  * Improve power consumption after shutdown on Mini (fix headphone power management logic)\n  * Support for MVP alarm functionality\n  * Any button press can be used to cancel a sounding alarm\n  * Fix nightlight brightness not changing while playing content\n\nYoto OS v2.9.13 (20th October 2022)\n\n  * Fixed issue with the right button not cancelling setup mode\n  * Fixed issue with audio not always playing on wired headphones\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nContrôlez votre lecteur (https://support.yotoplay.com/fr/controlez-votre-lecteur-SyGKKj7zg)\nciteturn816search7 [wordlim: 200] Published: last month; Crawled: 2 weeks ago;   * Appuyer de nouveau : pour lancer la Radio Yoto (et une fois de plus pour revenir à l'horloge).\n\n  * Maintenir enfoncé environ 3 secondes : (lorsque l'horloge est affichée) pour ouvrir le menu Bluetooth. Tournez ensuite le bouton de droite pour choisir, puis appuyez pour confirmer. [ESPACE LIEN - Utiliser un casque avec votre Yoto]\n\n### Bouton rotatif orange de droite\n\nLorsqu'une carte est insérée :\n\n  * Appuyer : pour passer à la piste ou au chapitre suivant.\n\n  * Tourner : pour naviguer en avant ou en arrière à travers les pistes et les chapitres.\n\n  * Maintenir enfoncé (plus d'1 seconde) : pour avancer rapidement pendant la lecture.\n\nSans aucune carte insérée :\n\n  * Appuyer une fois : pour lancer Yoto Journal (nécessite d'être connecté au Wi-Fi).\n\n  * Appuyer de nouveau : pour lancer la Radio Yoto (et une fois de plus pour revenir à l'horloge).\n\n### Yoto Player uniquement — Mode veilleuse (lecteur posé face vers le bas) :\n\n  * Tourner : vers la droite pour augmenter la luminosité de la veilleuse (ou l'allumer), vers la gauche pour la baisser jusqu'à l'éteindre complètement.\n\n> 💡 Astuce de pro : Vous pouvez personnaliser l'action du bouton de droite pour le mode Jour et le mode Nuit directement depuis l'application Yoto (rendez-vous dans l'onglet Paramètres de votre lecteur).\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nYoto App updates (https://support.yotoplay.com/en_gb/yoto-app-updates-BJZeKFsQGg)\nciteturn816search8 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3 months ago; Crawled: last week; from player settings set up to 10 alarms to sound on your player (turn off the alarm by pressing any button on the player) ...   * Maxi player: A player seek bar visibility fix when playing Yoto Daily / Mini Journal from a right hand button press ...   * Player Settings: we have refreshed the Advanced section to follow the updates to the Day and Night mode sections in the last release ...   * Sleep Sounds: an exciting new feature coming to Yoto, Sleep Sounds is an addition to the My Library section of the app, and contains a selection of sounds to help sooth the restless when it’s time for bed.\n  * Bug fixes and performance improvements.\n\nYoto App v2.63 (14th Sept 2023)\n\n  * MYO: Upload and edit custom icons for your MYO tracks.\n  * Player Settings: We’ve refreshed the look of your player setting including dark mode support.\n  * Bug fixes and performance improvements.\n\nAndroid only\n\n  * Fixed crash affecting large file uploads.\n\nYoto App v2.62 (4th Sept 2023)\n\n  * MYO: Take a photo or upload an image to personalize your MYO playlists\n  * Alarms: Enable and disable individual alarms with the flick of a switch\n  * Coming soon in a future release: Upload your own custom pixel artwork to tracks MYO track\n  * Bug fixes and performance improvements\n\nYoto App v2.61 (14th Aug 2023)\n\n  * MYO: You can now upload any MP3s from your phone to a MYO playlist from within the app.\n  * Coming soon in a future release: Upload any artwork to your MYO playlist without going to the MYO webpage.\n\n  * Bug fixes and performance improvements.\n\nYoto App v2.60 (7th Aug 2023)\n\n  * MYO: Edit your MYO playlists in the app. Edit your playlist name and description. Rename, reorder and change the icons of your tracks.\n  * Coming soon in a future release: Upload any audio and artwork to your MYO playlist without going to the MYO webpage.\n  * Bug fixes and performance improvements.\n\nYoto App v2.59 (27th June 2023)\n\nYoto App v2.51 (13th Feb 2023)\n\n  * Player downloads: a new section to display the current card queued for download\n\n  * Numerous bug fixes and performance improvements\n\nYoto App v2.50 (2nd Feb 2023)\n\n  * Maxi player: card looping when playing on the phone. Player looping is coming soon!\n\n  * Maxi player: for streaming content a new animation indicates something is playing when the seek bar can't be displayed\n\n  * Pairing: a warning and confirmation when leaving an existing family to join another\n\n  * Numerous bug fixes and performance improvements\n\nYoto App v2.49 (18th Jan 2023)\n\n  * Bug fixes and performance improvements\n\nYoto App v2.48 (16th Jan 2023)\n\n  * Bug fixes and performance improvements\n\nYoto App v2.47 (12th Dec 2022)\n\n  * Menu: a troubleshooting test to ensure your network can get through to the Yoto cloud\n\n  * Store tab: added a club link to take you to the club page on the website\n\n  * Numerous bug fixes and performance improvements\n\nYoto App v2.46 (1st Dec 2022)\n\n  * ALARMS!! from player settings set up to 10 alarms to sound on your player (turn off the alarm by pressing any button on the player)\n  * Menu tab:switch between modes from the app menu\n  * Numerous bug fixes and performance improvements\n\nYoto App v2.45 (22nd Nov 2022)\n\n  * ALARMS!! from player settings set up to 10 alarms to sound on your player (your player must be on beta).\n  * Player settings: player downloads view improvements\n  * Maxi player: time remaining added to the track position scrubber\n  * Maxi player: 'Scan a card' moved into the three dots menu\n  * Menu tab: light restyle\n  * Store tab: dark mode\n  * Voice recording permissions fix for Android 13\n  * Fix for missing right hand button section for Android 6 and 7\n  * Numerous bug fixes and performance improvements\n\nYoto App v2.44 (14th Oct 2022)\n\n  * Maxi Player: pause & resume controls so you can pause a card for a moment without then having to find it in the library again\n  * Maxi Player: added more support for dark mode in the app\n  * Card details: volume control and a player picker\n  * Library: new empty state designs\n  * Players: new logged out and empty state designs\n  * Numerous bug fixes and performance improvements\n\nYoto App v2.43 (16th Sept 2022)\n\nYoto App v2.34 (12th Dec 2021)\n\n  * Sleep timer: set a timer to stop your Player or Mini playing after a set period of minutes\n  * Remove a Library card: hide purchases from the app and then add them back in by playing them again\n  * Player MAC address: find your Player MAC address in Player settings\n  * Numerous bug fixes and performance improvements\n\nYoto App v2.33 (24th Nov 2021)\n\n  * Player and app: visibility of what your Player or Mini is doing, its current and maximum volume, and what is playing on it\n  * App expanded player screen: a refreshed design with space for some upcoming features\n  * Track listings screen: a refreshed design and the ability to start individual tracks playing on your Player or Mini from the app\n  * Yoto Mini: setup screens for our new portable player\n  * Lots of bug fixes and performance improvements behind the scenes\n\nYoto App v2.32 (5th Oct 2021)\n\n  * Numerous bug fixes and performance improvements\n\nYoto App v2.31 (2nd Sept 2021)\n\n  * Player Settings: we have refreshed the Advanced section to follow the updates to the Day and Night mode sections in the last release\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n4ème Generation Yoto FAQs (https://support.yotoplay.com/fr/4me-generation-yoto-faqs-Byw2rlFzx)\nciteturn816search9 [wordlim: 200] Published: last month; Crawled: last week; Le bouton vert permet aux enfants d'accéder instantanément à leurs contenus audio préférés, sans avoir besoin de carte Yoto.\n\n## Comment fonctionne le bouton vert ?\n\nLe bouton vert permet aux enfants d'accéder instantanément à leurs contenus audio préférés, sans avoir besoin de carte Yoto. On tourne pour choisir, on appuie pour écouter ! \n\nDerrière ce bouton vert,  deux playlists: une pour la journée et une pour le soir, , qui peuvent accueillir jusqu'à 20 pistes audio chacune. Par défaut, le Mini Journal et la Radio Yoto sont inclus dans la sélection de jour, tandis que la Radio Douce Nuit prend le relais pour la nuit.\n\nCôté parents, tout est personnalisable depuis l'application Yoto. Vous pouvez y ajouter tout ce que vous voulez à ces deux playlists : des histoires, de la musique, des podcasts, des webradios, des bruits blancs, des minuteurs, des berceuses... et même vos propres enregistrements !\n\nUne fois ajoutés, les contenus se téléchargent directement sur le lecteur. Les enfants peuvent ainsi les écouter partout, même sans Wi-Fi. Attention, les contenus streamés comme les radios et certains podcasts nécessitent tout de même une connexion Internet. \n\n### Le bouton vert, mode d'emploi :\n\n  * Tournez-le pour faire défiler les pistes audios disponibles, vous verrez leurs illustrations s'afficher à l'écran.\n\n  * Appuyez pour lancer l'histoire ou la musique choisie.\n\n  * Appuyez à nouveau pour mettre sur pause.\n\n  * Maintenez le bouton enfoncé pour arrêter la lecture et réafficher l'horloge.\n\n  * Si rien n'est en cours d'écoute : un simple clic lance instantanément le premier titre de la playlist du moment. Par défaut, il s'agit du Mini Journal  la journée et de Radio Douce Nuit la nuit.\n\nÀ noter : Sur les anciennes générations du Yoto Player, il suffit d'une simple pression sur le bouton de droite pour profiter de cette fonction d'accès rapide.\n\nCôté parents, vous pouvez bien sûr modifier ce tout premier titre à n'importe quel moment depuis l'application Yoto !\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHow to use the sleep timer on your Yoto (https://support.yotoplay.com/en_gb/how-to-use-the-sleep-timer-on-your-yoto-HJ4gYKj7Mg)\nciteturn816search10 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3 months ago; Crawled: last week; ## How to use the sleep timer on your Yoto\n\n## How to use the sleep timer on your Yoto\n\nJuly 20 2026 9:44am\n\n#### The Sleep Timer feature is perfect for bedtimes, but it can be useful for other situations too!\n\nTo set your player to stop playing after a set time, simply follow these simple steps: \n\n1) Tap the “now playing” bar at the base of the screen to open the Maxi Player view.\n\nImage: Yoto app - now playing bar\n\n2) Tap the ‘moon and stars’ icon at the top of the screen.\n\nImage: Yoto app - moon and stars icon\n\n3) Set your time.\n\nImage: Yoto app - select time\n\n4) Once the timer has elapsed, your player will stop playing. \n\nImage: Yoto app - timer elapsed\n\nDon’t worry if you’ve changed cards or played something different while the timer is running, it will keep running until it runs out, or until you set it to 'off'.\n\nTo set your sleep timer off, simply tap the moon and stars icon again and select ‘off’.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHow to check if your Yoto player is online (https://support.yotoplay.com/en_gb/how-to-check-if-your-yoto-player-is-online-rJ_A_Ki7Mx)\nciteturn816search11 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3 months ago; Crawled: last week; When your player is online, the sun or moon icon will be displayed (depending on whether your Yoto is currently in 'day' mode or 'night' mode), and the time will be displayed in red.\n\n## How to check if your Yoto player is online\n\n#### There are several reasons why you may need to know if your player is currently online.\n\nDownloading content to the player\n\nThe player needs to be online to download and store locally the audio content for each card. So to play a card for the first time, your player needs to be online.\n\nStreaming content\n\nSome cards or content, like radio, always need a connection to play, so if your player is offline, this content won't work.\n\nAdding new Wi-Fi details\n\nIf you want to add new Wi-Fi details to your player, so it can access another network, you can only do this if your player is offline.\n\nHow to tell if your player is online\n\nWhen your player is online, the sun or moon icon will be displayed (depending on whether your Yoto is currently in 'day' mode or 'night' mode), and the time will be displayed in red. \n\nIf the time is displayed in white, this means Yoto Player is currently offline.\n\nSome other icons you may see, and what they mean\n\nThe green Yoto Face icon means that your player is connected to Wi-Fi but not connected to the internet - this can happen if your internet connection is down.\n\nImage: Yoto mini - green Yoto face display\n\nWhen the white Yoto Face icon doesn't go away, it means that your player is offline, and it can’t see what the time is  - please follow the setup flow in the Yoto app to get your player online.\n\nImage: Yoto mini - white Yoto face display\n\nClick here for more information on all the display icons and what they mean.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInternal Error ()\nciteturn816view0 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://support.yotoplay.com/en_gb\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 1\nL0: Failed to fetch https://support.yotoplay.com/en_gb: (404) Not Found\n"
